# E2E Rules

## Do not change app logic for tests

* E2E work is **flows, subflows, credentials, and `testID`s only** — do not change product behavior, navigation, validation, or component logic to make a test pass.
* **Adapt the test to the app**, not the app to the test. Examples of forbidden changes: auto-closing menus on select, altering save/back navigation, changing form validation, or tweaking layouts/styles for Maestro.
* Allowed in app code: add or expose stable `testID`s (and minimal accessibility hooks if needed for detection). If a selector is hard to target, prefer a dedicated `testID` over behavior changes.
* If the app behaves correctly but the test fails, fix the **flow** (waits, scroll, tap target, env) — not business logic.

## Flows

* `yarn e2e` — main flow (`e2e/flows/main.yaml`), env from `e2e/config/credentials.yaml` via `scripts/run-e2e.js`.
* `yarn e2e:onboarding` — first-install onboarding only (`e2e/flows/onboarding/mode-screen.yaml`).
* Do not duplicate env vars in flow files; use `${VAR}` from credentials config.
* Do not use `onboarding-next-button` in the standard flow.

## Credentials (`e2e/config/credentials.yaml`)

* `E2E_ADMIN_EMAIL`, `E2E_ADMIN_NAME`, `E2E_ADMIN_PIN`
* `E2E_CHILD_USERNAME`, `E2E_CHILD1_NAME`, `E2E_CHILD_PIN`
* `E2E_CHILD2_USERNAME`, `E2E_CHILD2_NAME`, `E2E_CHILD2_AVATAR`, `E2E_CHILD2_PIN`
* `TASK_1_TITLE`, `TASK_1_AVATAR`, `TASK_1_REWARD`

## Selectors

* Use stable `testID` values; Maestro `id` selectors only.
* Never use visible text as selectors.

## Setup screen testIDs

* `onboarding-setup-screen`, `onboarding-setup-scroll`, `onboarding-multidevice-connect-*` (incl. `onboarding-multidevice-connect-pin-label`, `onboarding-multidevice-connect-pin-slots`, `onboarding-multidevice-connect-pin-slot-0`), `onboarding-section-*`, `onboarding-create-multidevice`, `onboarding-create-device-only`
* Never use `scrollUntilVisible` on `*-pin-slots` — if the testID is missing Maestro swipes until the app leaves the screen. Use `extendedWaitUntil` + tap `pin-label` to dismiss keyboard instead.

## Main app testIDs

* Tabs: `tab-tasks`, `tab-more`
* `tasks-screen`, `tasks-add-button`
* More: `more-menu-settings`, `more-menu-users`
* Settings: `settings-screen`, `settings-section-language`, `settings-language-en`
* Users / child form: `users-screen`, `users-add-child-button`, `users-child-list-item-{username}`, `child-form-*`, `child-form-delete`, `child-form-delete-confirm`, `child-form-delete-cancel`
* Child form: scroll to `users-add-child-button` before tap; never use `hideKeyboard` (Android back closes the form). Tap the next field immediately before each `inputText`. Form order: username → name → password → avatar → save — set password before scrolling to `child-form-avatar-${E2E_CHILD2_AVATAR}`.
* User switch: `user-switch-button`, `header-current-user-name`, `select-users-modal`, `user-switch-child-{username}`, `user-switch-parent-{slug}`, `user-switch-pin-slots`, `user-switch-pin-save`
* Child stars: `child-rewards-balance-value`
* Task form: `task-assignment-add-screen`, `task-assignment-form-scroll`, `task-assignment-children-select`, `task-assignment-children-select-menu`, `task-assignment-child-{username}`, `task-assignment-title`, `task-assignment-description`, `task-assignment-reward`, `task-assignment-reward-error`, `task-assignment-avatar-{value}`, `task-assignment-color-{name}`, `task-assignment-save`
* After selecting a child in `SelectMulti`, dismiss the menu by tapping outside (e.g. `task-assignment-title`) — not `task-assignment-children-select` again (double-taps the row and unchecks). Then **tap the target field again immediately before `inputText`** — never put `extendedWaitUntil` or scroll steps between `tapOn` and `inputText` on the same field (Android loses focus and text is not entered).
* On task form use `scrollUntilVisible` on `task-assignment-save` (short timeout) — avoid `swipe` from form edges (can trigger back navigation).
* Never use `hideKeyboard` or `eraseText` on the task form — on Android they trigger system back and leave the form. Dismiss keyboard by scrolling to and tapping `task-assignment-avatar-${TASK_1_AVATAR}` (not `task-assignment-description`, which can leave the keyboard open).
* Create-task flow: select child → title `${TASK_1_TITLE}` → description `Description` → tap `task-assignment-avatar-${TASK_1_AVATAR}` → save (reward empty) → scroll up → assert `task-assignment-reward-error` → reward `${TASK_1_REWARD}` → tap avatar again → save → assert task in list.
* Task list: `task-list-item-{title}`, `task-list-item-{title}-status-pending|completed|approved|approve|reject`
* `screen-header-back`

## Subflows

* `set-language-english.yaml`
* `create-child2.yaml`
* `create-task1-for-tarecitaschild1.yaml`
* `change-user.yaml` (params: `USER_SWITCH_TARGET`, `USER_SWITCH_PIN`)
* `change-user-to-child1.yaml`, `change-user-to-mama.yaml`
* `delete-child2.yaml` — switch to admin, open Users, delete `${E2E_CHILD2_USERNAME}`, assert removed from list
